Concrete LLVM execution now passes all prompt examples plus two extra even/odd-length cases. The first test harness used Python identity checks (`is True`), which this intentionally small semantics does not define for booleans; I corrected the harness to test truthiness without changing the solution. Next I’m compiling the symbolic definition and checking the universal string claim.
Inspected the semantics, implemented the direct reverse-equality solution, generated its constructor term, and passed concrete LLVM tests.
  ✓ Inspect prompt, translator, and reference semantics
  ✓ Implement solution.py and generate solution.mpy
  → Build K execution and proof definitions
  • Run concrete tests and prove all claims
  • Finalize prove.sh and verify deliverables
